.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt SCHED_4BSD 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sched_4bsd
.Nd "4.4BSD scheduler"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "options SCHED_4BSD"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
scheduler
is the traditional system scheduler, providing both high throughput and solid
interactive response in the presence of load.
.Pp
Common scheduler sysctls are documented in
.Xr scheduler 4 .
.Pp
The following sysctls are relevant to the operation of
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va kern.sched.4bsd.quantum
The length of the timeshare quantum in microseconds.
.It Va kern.sched.4bsd.slice
The length of the timeshare quantum in statclock ticks.
.El
.Pp
The following sysctls are available only on SMP systems:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va kern.sched.4bsd.runq_fuzz
The number of threads to examine in the highest-priority queue in search for a
thread that last ran on the current CPU.
If no such thread exists, the first thread is chosen.
Negative values and 0 are treated like 1 (the default), i.e., the first thread
in queue is always chosen.
.It Va kern.sched.4bsd.ipiwakeup.enabled
Whether to send an inter-processor interrupt (IPI) to an idle CPU when a
thread is woken up.
.It Va kern.sched.4bsd.ipiwakeup.usemask
Whether to use the mask of idle CPUs when forwarding wakeups.
.It Va kern.sched.4bsd.ipiwakeup.useloop
Whether to search for idle CPUs in a loop when forwarding wakeups.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr scheduler 4 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
scheduler has been present, in various forms, since the inception of
.Bx .
.Sh BUGS
While a highly robust and time-tested scheduler,
.Nm
lacks specific knowledge of how to schedule advantageously in non-symmetric
processor configurations, such as hyper-threading.
